+\subsection{Candidate pools and exact enumeration}\label{sec:p2pools}
+La and Ti, in that site order, minimize predicted violation in both candidate pools. We fix $X=\mathrm{NO_2}$, the dataset label for two O atoms and one N atom. For each ordered cation pair $(a,b)$, its cost $W_{ab}$ is the mean prediction of the 20 H-soft members fitted using files 02 and 03. Known training compositions also receive predictions.
+
+Figure~\ref{fig:p2pipeline} shows which pairs remain eligible. File 07 contains all $52\times52$ pairs. File 11 contains the 529 pairs in this slice of the unlabeled test file 04; the other 2,175 pairs occur in files 02 or 03. Hatching marks forbidden pairs. Steps show the observed bin shares; the smooth curves interpolate their centres.
+\paperfigure{P2/plates/P2-F1_data_pipeline.pdf}{Predicted violation in the full and blind pools}{fig:p2pipeline}
+
+Table~\ref{tab:p2pools} gives the nearest competitor in each pool. Here and below, original regret is a candidate's predicted violation minus the least predicted violation among allowed candidates in the same pool.
+\begin{table}[!htb]
+\centering
+\caption{Minima and runners-up in the two pools}\label{tab:p2pools}
+\begin{tabular}{@{}lrlrlr@{}}
+\toprule
+Pool & Pairs & Minimum & $\widehat V_{\min}$ & Runner-up & Gap\\
+\midrule
+Full (07) & 2,704 & LaTiO$_2$N & 1.839047 & ScTiO$_2$N & 0.416697\\
+Blind (11) & 529 & LaTiO$_2$N & 1.839047 & SrTaO$_2$N & 0.465139\\
+\bottomrule
+\end{tabular}
+\end{table}
+
+LaTiO$_2$N has an experimental counterpart. Kasahara et al. measured hydrogen and oxygen evolution in separate visible-light reactions with a sacrificial donor and acceptor, respectively~\cite{kasahara2002}. The blind pool contains no joint measurement of the five contest criteria for this candidate. Figure~\ref{fig:p2crystal} shows the Ti coordination in an external structure~\cite{mp1222738}.
+\paperfigure{P2/plates/P2-A1_crystal_orientations.pdf}{Three views of the LaTiO$_2$N coordination network}{fig:p2crystal}
