+\subsection{Encoding and precision checks}\label{app:p2encoding}
+For the short-chain certificate, fix the reference spin to $+1$. Extending a prefix ending in spin $s$ by spin $t$ at position $j$ adds $-2t(J_{j,\mathrm{ref}}+J_{j-1,j}s)$; the first position has only its reference term. Keep the smaller energy for each pair of last spin and violation flag. The flag records whether a minus-to-plus transition has occurred.
+
+Figure~\ref{fig:p2graph} separates the within-register penalties from the A--B lookup in Eq.~\eqref{eq:p2qubo}. Each sector contains 13 adjacent spins in the register order. The shared reference is included. Bundle width scales with the square root of total absolute weight; all 5,459 nonzero edges are shown (threshold zero). The layout represents the logical matrix.
+\paperfigure{P2/plates/P2-A2_grouped_lookup.pdf}{Couplings within and between the two registers}{fig:p2graph}
+
+Figure~\ref{fig:p2precision} separates legality from the ordering of the allowed candidates. A counterexample supplies an illegal state with energy at or below the allowed minimum; an unresolved certificate leaves legality open. Cell values give the largest original regret among allowed integer minima. RC denotes row--column reparameterization.
+
+ Removing the lookup costs in the direct 8-bit blind matrix changes 312 matrix entries. This control distinguishes partial loss of resolution from complete loss of cost dependence.
+\paperfigure{P2/plates/P2-A7_precision_audit.pdf}{Precision and legality of the lookup encoding}{fig:p2precision}
